          body: 'A living cell is roughly 70 per cent water by mass, and almost every reaction you will meet in this course happens in a watery solution. Life on Earth is thought to have begun in water, and when scientists search other planets for life, they look first for liquid water. Why is this plain molecule, H₂O, so special? The answer is not mysterious. It comes from two simple facts: the shape of the molecule and an uneven sharing of electrons. Once you understand those two facts, the strange behaviour of water – ice that floats, insects that walk on ponds, sweat that cools you – all follows.',
