          body: 'After water, almost everything in your body is built on carbon. Sugars, fats, proteins and DNA are all organic molecules, meaning carbon-based molecules that usually also contain hydrogen. Why carbon? An atom of carbon has four electrons in its outer shell, so it forms four covalent bonds, in which atoms share electron pairs. Four bonds point in four directions, like the corners of a pyramid, so carbon can join to other carbons and to hydrogen, oxygen, nitrogen, phosphorus and sulfur. This makes enormous variety possible: from methane, with one carbon, to a human chromosome with hundreds of millions.',
